      "writtenOn": "2026-08-02T16:40:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, # is prefix-stripping, not a default — I overplayed that. But the real issue is separation of concerns: load_config.sh owns parsing, yet run-ci.sh still does its own string transformation (${VAR#ubuntu:}) on an already-loaded value. That\u0027s leaky abstraction — the consumer now encodes an assumption about the JSON\u0027s format. If the format changes (as you proposed — u14.04, alma10, etc.), this strip silently does the wrong thing (or nothing) instead of failing loudly, and someone has to go hunting through run-ci.sh to figure out why a container tag looks wrong.\n\nSuggestion: move the stripping into load_config.sh and export a clean derived value. Consumers should only ever consume finished config — zero parsing logic downstream, single source of truth fully enforced by JSON and load_config.sh.",
      "parentUuid": "91996cac_7a650cde",
